{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMC9GVLRkcwRteszfqRu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RHXrkBXGpdx7xm4nLPRk4i","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"cases":[{"id":"inherited_session_rejection","met":true,"report_quote":"The attacker sends `GET /mcp` with `mcp-session-id: constructor`, `__proto__` or `toString`.","reason":"The report gives the full dataflow. The plain-object `sessions` lookup at :17/:22 returns an inherited truthy value, so the 404 check is bypassed. `handleRequest` is then undefined, and the TypeError is thrown in an async handler that Express 4 doesn't catch. Node 20 default throw mode makes it an uncaught exception. It states the bearer-secret prerequisite and cites the file lines and research. It frames the crash as inference from source, not a tested result."},{"id":"auth_boundary","met":true,"report_quote":"Middleware on `/mcp` (also matches `/mcp/init`)","reason":"The report treats the bearer middleware as gating all /mcp routes, including init. It makes no unauthenticated-attack claim and invents no OAuth audience gap. It limits F1 to the single trusted principal's key."},{"id":"runtime_scope","met":true,"report_quote":"**Behavior tested: none.** This was a read-only source review.","reason":"The report makes no runtime or crash measurement claims. It lists host audit, ingress/TLS, supervision and the secret store as unknown external controls."},{"id":"coverage_get","met":true,"report_quote":"| `GET /mcp` and `DELETE /mcp` | Session lookup, error handling | F1 |","reason":"The GET handler's session lookup and its missing error handling are assessed in F1 with line evidence (:16-20, :17, :18, :19)."},{"id":"coverage_delete","met":true,"report_quote":"`:21-25` | Gated, plus a session lookup","reason":"The inventory lists the DELETE handler at :21-25, and F1 cites :22, :23 and :24 for the same flaw. F2 separately assesses DELETE's failure to remove sessions."},